#### Phase 2: Plugin Development Kit

**Step 1: Create Plugin Base Classes**

```csharp
public abstract class PluginBase : IPlugin
{
    protected ILogger Logger { get; private set; }
    protected IConfiguration Configuration { get; private set; }

    public abstract string PluginId { get; }
    public abstract string Name { get; }
    public abstract Version Version { get; }
    public abstract PluginMetadata Metadata { get; }

    public virtual async Task InitializeAsync(IPluginContext context)
    {
        Logger = context.Logger;
        Configuration = context.Configuration;
        await OnInitializeAsync(context);
    }

    protected virtual Task OnInitializeAsync(IPluginContext context)
    {
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    public abstract Task<PluginResult> ExecuteAsync(IExecutionContext executionContext);

    public virtual void Dispose()
    {
        // Cleanup resources
    }
}
```

**Step 2: Provide Project Template**

Create Visual Studio/dotnet template:
```xml
<!-- Plugin.csproj -->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net6.0</TargetFramework>
    <EnableDynamicLoading>true</EnableDynamicLoading>
    <GeneratePluginManifest>true</GeneratePluginManifest>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Gainwell.Extensions.PluginSDK" Version="1.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PluginMetadata Include="plugin.json" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
```

**Step 3: Document Plugin Development Guidelines**
- Plugin naming conventions
- Metadata requirements
- Testing strategies
- Security best practices
- Performance guidelines

