### Real-World Example 1

**State-Specific Claims Edit Implementation**

A state Medicaid agency requires specialized claims editing logic that complies with state-specific legislation (AB-109 for behavioral health services).

**Problem:** Core product cannot contain every state's unique editing rules. State A needs 47 unique edits, State B needs 63 different edits.

**Solution:**

```csharp
// State A Plugin Implementation
[Plugin("com.gainwell.mmis.statea.claims.edits")]
public class StateAClaimsEditPlugin : PluginBase, IClaimsEditingPlugin
{
    private readonly IStateARulesEngine _rulesEngine;
    private readonly ILogger<StateAClaimsEditPlugin> _logger;

    public override string PluginId => "com.gainwell.mmis.statea.claims.edits";
    public override Version Version => new Version(3, 2, 1);

    public async Task<EditResult> ApplyEditsAsync(Claim claim, EditContext context)
    {
        var results = new List<EditResult>();

        // State A Edit SA-4521: AB-109 Behavioral Health Screening
        if (claim.ServiceType == "BehavioralHealth" &&
            claim.ServiceDate >= new DateTime(2023, 7, 1))
        {
            var screeningResult = await _rulesEngine.ApplyAB109ScreeningAsync(claim);
            results.Add(screeningResult);
        }

        // State A Edit SA-2101: Enhanced Provider Credentialing
        var providerStatus = await ValidateStateAProviderAsync(claim.ProviderId);
        if (!providerStatus.IsValid)
        {
            results.Add(EditResult.Fail("SA-2101",
                "Provider must complete State A credentialing"));
        }

        return EditResult.Combine(results);
    }
}
```

**Deployment:**
- Plugin deployed only to State A tenant (`/plugins/state-a/claims-edits/`)
- Core product invokes plugin at designated extension point
- State A updates editing rules quarterly without core product changes

**Results:**
- State-specific logic isolated from core product
- Independent deployment cycle (8 releases/year vs 3 for core)
- 60% reduction in core product complexity

