### Real-World Example 2

**Multi-Tenant Reporting with Tenant-Specific Plugins**

Gainwell hosts a multi-tenant MMIS platform serving 8 states in a shared Azure environment. Each state requires unique regulatory reports.

**Architecture:**

```
Shared Application Host (Azure App Service)
├── Core Reporting Engine
├── /plugins/tenant-statea/
│   ├── StateA.Reports.CHIP.dll
│   └── StateA.Reports.Utilization.dll
├── /plugins/tenant-stateb/
│   ├── StateB.Reports.ManagedCare.dll
│   └── StateB.Reports.Financial.dll
└── /plugins/tenant-statec/
    └── StateC.Reports.Compliance.dll
```

**Implementation:**

```csharp
public class MultiTenantReportingEngine
{
    private readonly IPluginHost _pluginHost;
    private readonly ITenantResolver _tenantResolver;

    public async Task<Report> GenerateReportAsync(
        HttpContext context,
        string reportType,
        ReportParameters parameters)
    {
        // Resolve tenant from request context
        var tenantId = await _tenantResolver.GetTenantIdAsync(context);

        // Load tenant-specific plugins only
        var tenantPlugins = await _pluginHost.GetPluginsForTenantAsync(
            tenantId,
            typeof(IReportGeneratorPlugin));

        // Find plugin for requested report
        var reportPlugin = tenantPlugins
            .OfType<IReportGeneratorPlugin>()
            .FirstOrDefault(p => p.SupportsReportType(reportType));

        if (reportPlugin != null)
        {
            return await reportPlugin.GenerateReportAsync(parameters);
        }

        // Fallback to standard reports
        return await GenerateStandardReportAsync(reportType, parameters);
    }
}
```

**Security & Isolation:**
- Each tenant's plugins loaded in isolated AssemblyLoadContext
- State A cannot access State B plugin code or data
- Tenant-specific database connections injected per plugin
- IP isolation maintained through folder-level access control

**Benefits:**
- Single codebase serves 8 states
- Each state independently deploys reporting plugins
- Shared infrastructure reduces hosting costs by 45%
- Zero cross-contamination of state-specific code

